# Story 6: Splitting Panes (45s)
# Hook: Need more terminals? Split your panes -- columns and rows.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-06-splitting-panes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Need more terminals? Split your panes -- columns and rows.

[00:03.0 --> 00:06.0]
Start rysh -- you get one tab, one pane.

[00:06.0 --> 00:12.0]
Ctrl+P enters pane mode. Press n to split right -- creating a second column.

[00:12.0 --> 00:18.0]
Now you have two side-by-side panes. Each is independent.

[00:18.0 --> 00:25.0]
Ctrl+P again, then v splits down -- a new row in the same column.

[00:25.0 --> 00:33.0]
Tab back to another pane, then Ctrl+P n again for a third column.

[00:33.0 --> 00:40.0]
Tab cycles through every pane. You now have a 3-column layout with one column split into rows.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
Split horizontally with n, vertically with v. Combine them however you like.

